{"name":"Rusty Red","hex":"#af2f0d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rusty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Marked or corroded by rust. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Of the rust color, reddish or reddish-brown."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A gun or in particular an old or worn one."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rusty"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Turkestan cockroach","blocks":[{"text":"Periplaneta lateralis, commonly known as the Turkestan cockroach, red runner cockroach, or rusty red cockroach, is a primarily outdoor-dwelling cockroach native to an area stretching from northern Africa to Central Asia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Turkestan_Cockroach%2C_Leo_Nature_Trail%2C_Malibu%2C_CA%2C_US_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_548136297.jpg/330px-Turkestan_Cockroach%2C_Leo_Nature_Trail%2C_Malibu%2C_CA%2C_US_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_548136297.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turkestan_cockroach"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Turkestan_Cockroach%2C_Valencia%2C_Santa_Clarita%2C_CA%2C_USA_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_209200427_%28closeup%29.jpg/500px-Turkestan_Cockroach%2C_Valencia%2C_Santa_Clarita%2C_CA%2C_USA_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_209200427_%28closeup%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Turkestan_Cockroach%2C_Valencia%2C_Santa_Clarita%2C_CA%2C_USA_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_209200427_%28closeup%29.jpg/1280px-Turkestan_Cockroach%2C_Valencia%2C_Santa_Clarita%2C_CA%2C_USA_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_209200427_%28closeup%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Turkestan_Cockroach%2C_Valencia%2C_Santa_Clarita%2C_CA%2C_USA_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_209200427_%28closeup%29.jpg/500px-Turkestan_Cockroach%2C_Valencia%2C_Santa_Clarita%2C_CA%2C_USA_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_209200427_%28closeup%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATurkestan_Cockroach%2C_Valencia%2C_Santa_Clarita%2C_CA%2C_USA_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_209200427_(closeup).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Turkestan_Cockroach%2C_Los_Angeles_County%2C_US-CA%2C_US_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_145780992.jpg/250px-Turkestan_Cockroach%2C_Los_Angeles_County%2C_US-